<title>ITALY: Montedison '97 Jan-May op margin rises.</title>
<headline>Montedison '97 Jan-May op margin rises.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian agri-industrial group Montedison saw its gross operating margin rise 13.5 percent to 1.5 trillion lire ($889.6 million) in the first five months of this year, managing director Enrico Bondi said.</p>
<p>Bondi told the annual shareholders meeting here sales in the January to May period had risen 13 percent on the same 1996 period to 11.2 trillion lire. ($ = 1686 Italian Lire)</p>
